WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.801
-Welcome back, John.
It's always great to see you.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.033
You look great, bud.
-It's nice to be here, thanks.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.434
-Yeah, it is Nana Week.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.467
We're talking about
nanas and highlighting --

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.934
spotlighting grandmothers.
-Congratulations.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:13.100
-Yeah, thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.934
Do you have any memories
of your grandma?

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.000
-You're presuming they're dead.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.968
-Is she alive? I'm so sorry.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:25.400
-No, she is dead.
-Okay.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.601
I shouldn't have asked that,
I'm so sorry.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:34.334
-It's just the idea you went
leaning in so hard

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.434
with "Any memories?"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:37.634
-That's not what I meant --

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.334
-It was supposed to be
a high-risk strategy,

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.434
but you stuck the landing.
She died.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.100
-Okay, no, I didn't --
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.467
-A while ago.
And I do -- Yes, she was great.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.834
She was from Liverpool, which is
where all my family is from.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:50.234
And she loved comedy.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.434
And right towards the end,

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.634
she got into a bit of
a scuffle with --

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:57.100
in her old people's home.
-No.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.801
-Yeah, she walked around
in a nighty a lot, all day,

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.300
which, you know,
that's her right.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.334
Nighty, does that make sense?
Nighty?

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:05.968
-Yeah.
-Does that sound too Dickensian?

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.067
-No, a nighty. Yeah, sure.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.267
-Yeah, she walked around
in a nighty.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.734
And there was a woman
who lived opposite her

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.267
who took exception to this.

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:15.234
So she kind of came at her one
day, waggling a walking stick.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:19.367
She grabbed the stick, pulled it
towards her and then kind of --

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:22.601
honestly, kind of Will Smithed
an open-hand slap.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:28.601
[ Cheers and laughter ]

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:32.067
Yeah.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.534
The crazy thing is
Lupita Nyong'o

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:37.901
was there going, "Oh, [bleep]"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.067
She did. She did.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.334
There was definitely
a conversation about what --

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.367
"What do we do here?"

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.667
To which we -- Our thought was,
"You're allowed one."

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.634
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:50.934
-There was a -- She loved
the fact I did comedy

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:54.434
and there was a famous comedian
in Liverpool called Ken Dodd,

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:55.601
who you won't have heard of.

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:58.467
He was a very odd man who --

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:02.968
There's no way to explain this
in a concise way.

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.968
He used feather dusters
for his act.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.934
That's all --
Google it or don't.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.200
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.634
As part of his act,
he had two feather dusters?

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.033
-Yeah, that's right.
He used them to tell jokes.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.868
Anyway, the point is,
he was famously a tinker.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.200
Like, he used to spell pots
and pans as a young man.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.534
And he would talk about it a lot
on stage.

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:20.434
And he was -- he was a tinker
where my nan grew up.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:23.234
And she said, "Oh, you're
a comedian now like Doddy.

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:24.434
That's great. You know what?

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:26.400
He knocked on my door one day
and said,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.200
'Barb, you know,
if you buy this pan,

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.868
you'll never need to buy
another one.'"

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:32.167
And she said, "You know what?"

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:35.200
And she reached under her bed
and said, "I never did."

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.534
And she brought out a pan that
really should have been

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.367
thrown away about 55 years
previously.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:42.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.634
You can see lead paint
just flaking off it.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.634
Ken Dodd poisoned her
and my family.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.734
-Oh, my God.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.234
That's the whole point of
this story, yeah.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.801
-He's dead as well.
-No, sorry, yeah.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.300
-Just as long as we're listing
dead British people.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.501
-I want to ask, how are the --
How are the cute kids?

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.167
-They're alright. Yeah.
-They're good?

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.667
-They're great, yeah.
-They're what, six and three?

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.167
-Six and three now, yeah.

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:07.901
The 3-year-old has got really
into the Red Hot Chili Peppers.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:10.267
[ Laughter ]
I wasn't expecting it either.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.667
But he heard "Under the Bridge"
once

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:15.400
and has become obsessed with it.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.634
It's the only thing
he wants to be played,

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.634
it's the only thing he wants
to be sung to him at night,

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.267
and "Under the Bridge"
in particular.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.300
-"Under the Bridge"?
-"Under the Bridge."

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.767
You haven't heard
"Under the Bridge" until

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.767
you've heard a 3-year-old

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.834
gaze sorrowfully into
the mid-distance and said --

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:35.067
♪ Sometimes I feel like
I don't have a partner ♪

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:37.000
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, exactly.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.400
♪ Feel like my only fwend ♪

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.767
With a W. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.801
-Oh, my God.
-And can you imagine

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.334
a 3-year-old --
"I don't ever want to feel

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.534
like I did that day"?

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.400
What the [bleep] do you know
about pain?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.801
[ Laughter ]
At 3 years old.

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:54.033
I'll tell you about pain.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.767
Like you did what day?

00:03:56.767 --> 00:04:00.567
What day is such a bad memory
for you?

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:03.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:04.801
You're fine!

00:04:04.801 --> 00:04:07.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.467
He loves it. I was singing it
to him last night.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:14.100
He was like,
"Sing 'I don't want to feel.'"

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.167
Basically, "Under the Bridge"
is his "Baby Shark."

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:20.067
-Oh, I love that kid.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:23.133
"Last Week Tonight," you're back
into the studio, bud.

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.267
-Yes. We're back now, yeah.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:25.801
-Congrats.
-Thank you.

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.467
-The show is fantastic
as always.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.267
But now you're back
in the studio.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:32.300
And our pal Drew Barrymore is
your neighbor.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.534
-Yes. I met her -- I met her
when I was having

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:39.567
one of my first nasal swabs
early on in the pandemic.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.133
-You never forget your first.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:43.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.901
-Back when --
Kids don't understand.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.133
They used to go real deep.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.234
Not this kind of nose tickle
you're having now.

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:52.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:56.300
Anyway, she was -- you know,
she had a mask and a hat on.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.200
-Yeah.
-And she started yelling at me.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:02.334
And it took me like a few
seconds to realize who she was.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.834
Her show was just starting.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.801
And she was saying --
-You didn't know it was Drew?

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.434
-I gradually realized
it was her.

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:10.100
And then she was saying,
"I love late-night comedy."

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.367
And she said she been on
"The Johnny Carson Show."

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:13.767
And it was all happening
so fast.

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.467
I'm went, "How on Earth were you
on the Johnny Carson show?"

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:19.234
She looked at me and she said,
"I was in [bleep] 'E.T.'"

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:21.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:26.200
If I had known as a child that
Elliott's sister would one day

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.934
come out of that screen
and yell at me,

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:30.667
"I was in [bleep] 'E.T.,'"

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:33.834
I'd have been -- I would look
forward to every day

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.601
between then and that point.
-And now, yeah.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.701
-It was the first film
I ever saw.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:40.567
-I loved "E.T."
-It was -- I was carried --

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:43.067
The visceral memory I have is
being carried,

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:46.901
screaming tears,
as the credits were rolling

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:49.634
because I couldn't believe
he left, that E.T. left

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.000
and that Elliott
didn't go with him.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.400
That was the thing that
really broke my heart.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.734
-You thought Elliott
was going to go on --

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:56.801
-Of course!

00:05:56.801 --> 00:05:58.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.834
What's he staying for?
His family?

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.834
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, yes.

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:06.067
-An alien you just made a key
connection with

00:06:06.067 --> 00:06:08.834
is leaving, invites you to come.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.133
And you stayed?

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:11.934
Like, if we don't --
Even at that age,

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:14.667
I understood the fundamental
lore of rom-coms,

00:06:14.667 --> 00:06:17.234
if you can call "E.T." that,
which I'm not sure you can.

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:18.667
-No.
-Is you get on

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:20.367
the plane at the end.

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:23.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:25.467
-You're running --
Yes, you run after the thing --

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:27.868
-Go to him.
-Go to him, yeah.

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:29.868
-Go to him.
So yeah, I thought it was awful.

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:32.868
That little rainbow felt
sarcastic as it takes off.

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:35.801
I hope there's a director's cut
somewhere where

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:38.033
Elliott tells his family
and says, "Peace."

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:41.133
-Yeah, and goes to
space with E.T.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.067
-You know what I was going to
say to you, by the way,

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:45.667
last time you were on the show,
and I talked to you.

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:49.133
I said -- I was talking about --
I don't know how I got into it.

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:52.067
About meeting a dog.
-Oh, my God.

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:55.968
Oh, my -- That is -- Honestly,
you know, during the pandemic,

00:06:55.968 --> 00:06:59.167
it was hard to sometimes get
the laughter that you wanted

00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:00.601
and needed in that moment.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:04.334
That sentence that you stumbled
over gave me something

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:05.467
from deep, deep down.

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:06.467
[ Laughter ]
-I made you laugh --

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:07.734
-He was passing --

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:09.133
We were just having
conversation.

00:07:09.133 --> 00:07:10.734
And he said,
like it was nothing,

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:13.000
"Oh, I once met a famous dog
backstage

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.400
at a Kevin Hart concert."

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.701
And I remember thinking,
"Stop talking now

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:21.033
and unpack each ingredient
that you've presented there.

00:07:21.033 --> 00:07:24.434
Don't skim on like it's nothing

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.734
when what you presented
is a vignette to me."

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:28.167
-Yeah, you met a dog
at backstage --

00:07:28.167 --> 00:07:32.234
-You met a famous dog.
Not "a" dog. A "famous" dog.

00:07:32.234 --> 00:07:33.734
-Backstage at a Kevin --
-Backstage -- you did

00:07:33.734 --> 00:07:36.501
a meet-and-greet with
a famous dog backstage

00:07:36.501 --> 00:07:37.868
at a Kevin Hart concert.

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:39.801
All of those ingredients
separately are good.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:42.234
Together,
that is a "Chopped" episode

00:07:42.234 --> 00:07:43.501
that should make the final.

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.033
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:47.100
-Well, it really happened.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.601
And we tracked down
footage of this.

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:53.534
This is real. Here I am meeting
a dog named Jiffpom

00:07:53.534 --> 00:07:55.701
backstage at a Kevin Hart show.

00:07:56.601 --> 00:07:58.901
We'll figure it out, right?
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:01.067
And we're hanging out.

00:08:01.067 --> 00:08:03.400
I'll call you tomorrow.
It's good.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.434
-Look at that.
[ Applause ]

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:07.267
Wow, huh?
-Wow.

00:08:09.934 --> 00:08:12.267
-One of the things in that room
is looking at

00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:13.934
the other thinking,
"What are you doing here?"

00:08:13.934 --> 00:08:15.901
And it's -- it's not you, Jimmy.

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:17.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:18.601
-John Oliver, everybody.

00:08:18.601 --> 00:08:20.801
"Last Week Tonight
with John Oliver"

00:08:20.801 --> 00:08:23.467
airs Sundays at 11:00 p.m.
on HBO.

